  "name": "sim_axis0_gtower_gradient_cascade",
  "classification": "classical_baseline",
  "claim": "As a matrix descends the G-tower GL->O->SO, the distinguishability cost I_c (Axis 0) decreases monotonically. Each projection step eliminates degrees of freedom. The residual ||A - proj(A)||_F is the Axis 0 cost at that transition. The identity matrix is the ground state and autograd on the residual norm is the Axis 0 gradient.",
  "divergence_log": "Classical foundation baseline: the G-tower gradient cascade remains a bounded matrix-algebraic Axis 0 doctrine. The legacy GL->O->SO residual and monotonicity claims are preserved, and the same cascade is now grounded in the deep Axis 0 shell/topology/symbolic/solver/manifold contract instead of a partial/deferred tool header.",
